The function to divide a linked list into two separate lists, one containing all the even numbers and the other containing all the odd numbers, is:

```python
def divide(head):
    resStart = None
    resEnd = None
    curr = head
    prev = None

    while curr is not None:
        if curr.data % 2 == 0:
            if prev is not None:
                prev.next = curr.next
            else:
                head = curr.next
            if resStart is None:
                resStart = curr
                resEnd = resStart
            else:
                resEnd.next = curr
                resEnd = resEnd.next
            curr = curr.next
        else:
            prev = curr
            curr = curr.next

    if resStart is None:
        return head
    resEnd.next = head
    return resStart
```

This function iterates through the linked list, separating even and odd nodes into two separate lists. If there are no even nodes, it returns the original list.
